    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d59">

                <pb facs="0100" n="82" sameAs="frus:frus1946v02/pg82"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 EW (Peace)/4–1946</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The British Ambassador</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Halifax</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-04-19">April 19, 1946</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Secretary of State</hi>, Mr. Bevin has asked
                    me to send you a reply to the message which you sent him asking if he could
                    discuss informally with you in Paris the proposed German disarmament clauses
                    which you sent to him in mid-February.<anchor n="14" xml:id="d59-f1"/> Mr. Bevin
                    says that the Cabinet have authorised him to tell you that His Majesty’s
                    Government warmly welcome your proposal on German disarmament and consider that
                    your draft provides a most useful basis for further discussion. Mr. Bevin will
                    be very happy to discuss the matter with you informally in Paris. He will not be
                    accompanied by military experts but, if necessary, these could be summoned at
                    short notice. Mr. Bevin feels sure that you and he can have some useful
                    discussion on the general lines of your proposal.</p>
                <p>Believe me [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Halifax</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d59-f1" n="14" xml:id="d59-f1-content">
                <p>The Secretary’s message under reference here is quoted in footnote 83, <ref
